The native MXFP6 integration, optional LM head search and source profile
contain code derived from the vLLM project and the downstream optimization
series ending at 8983c0369e, under Apache-2.0. Original file notices are retained.

The optional NVFP4 head uses B12X-derived kernels vendored by FlashInfer.
These kernels retain their upstream notices and licenses in FlashInfer;
the standalone B12X package is not required by this runtime.
Earlier EXL3 implementations and their original notices are retained in Git
history, not in the current source tree or wheel.

MXFP6 SM120 is an optional external runtime dependency provided by the
mxfp6-sm120 package. Its CUDA source code is not distributed in this package and
remains subject to the BSD 3-Clause License.

The MXFP6 workspace warmup integration follows the public mxfp6_sm120 vLLM
example and is adapted as Apache-2.0 framework glue for vLLM Mach.

The version-locked FlashInfer profile contains a small patch derived from the
FlashInfer project, which is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The optional native/lossless_prefill extension contains a frozen collective
header and operations derived from FlashInfer under Apache-2.0, with a
lossless BF16 peer-read codec. It is built separately from the Python wheel.

The optional native/owner_prefill extension also contains a collective header
derived from FlashInfer under Apache-2.0, with owner-row communication and
local MLP operations. Original header notices are retained. It is built
separately from the Python wheel.

The optional mxfp6/gdn persistent CUDA kernel and host support are derived
from FlashInfer (historical Mach snapshot 8c5021a), under Apache-2.0.
Original notices are retained; the kernel now treats vLLM 0.29 null slot zero
as padding. BA overlap scheduling is adapted from the earlier Mach profile.

The MXFP6 MoE adapter and Quark MoE patch are adapted from the Apache-2.0
vLLM example in Nekofish-L/mxfp6_sm120, revision
cd4e964c391fcb8aaf1a27d28a63d778e3a38ece. Original notices are retained.
The CUDA kernels remain in the external mxfp6-sm120 dependency.
